# PART I — CORE LANGUAGE AND NATIVE FOUNDATION

# 1. LANGUAGE IDENTITY, GOVERNANCE AND ARCHITECTURE

## 1.1 Language classification

Paracine is a statically typed, compiled, general-purpose native programming language.

Its language architecture combines:

- Deterministic semantic analysis.
- Explicit type relationships.
- Ownership-based memory management.
- Inferred nonlexical borrowing.
- Native value representations.
- Defined integer arithmetic.
- Explicit computational effects.
- Structured concurrency.
- Recoverable error values.
- Terminal failure semantics.
- Generics and structural capabilities.
- Compile-time evaluation.
- Advanced encapsulation and isolation.
- Typed computational graphs.
- Verified optimization.
- Direct machine-code generation.

The language does not require garbage collection, virtual-machine interpretation, mandatory heap-backed closures, foreign-language transpilation or external compilation infrastructure.

## 1.2 Canonical native compilation

The compiler operates through the following production pipeline:

