# PART VI — PITEL PROGRESSIVE INTELLIGENCE

# 30. SIX-STAGE PROGRESSIVE SEMANTIC ARCHITECTURE

PITEL accelerates SAGE's semantic reasoning, knowledge maintenance, proof processing and optimization search.

It is a throughput architecture, not an alternative semantic authority.

## Stage I — Immediate Recognition

PITEL recognizes tokens, declarations, scopes, direct dependencies, literals and immediately established facts.

## Stage II — Relational Analysis

PITEL resolves connected type, ownership, effect, resource, Capsule, Family, Chain and contract relationships.

## Stage III — Deductive Expansion

PITEL applies semantic inference, constraint propagation, abstract interpretation and fixed-point analysis.

## Stage IV — Speculative Exploration

PITEL explores candidate optimization and architectural routes within explicit budgets.

## Stage V — Authoritative Verification

PITEL schedules and processes required proof obligations, rejecting unsound or unsupported conclusions.

## Stage VI — Consolidation and Native Realization

PITEL reuses verified knowledge, deduplicates conclusions, updates the Blueprint and supplies verified inputs to native compilation.

## 30.1 Permanent PITEL law

**Accelerate reasoning without weakening proof. Accelerate inference without inventing facts. Accelerate compilation without changing program meaning.**

